Write the persona's technical opinion on the topic. Ground factual claims in
the evidence above. Cite evidence using its bracketed reference: either the
number shown above (for example `[2]`) or the paper identifier already in the
title (for example `[2604.21330]`). An evidence number `[n]` refers to item `n`
of the evidence list; never invent a reference that is not listed above. If any
evidence cuts against the persona's stance, acknowledge that counter-evidence
explicitly before explaining the persona's conclusion. Do not mention the
persona's name merely to create an artificial difference in output.